# Effective .dockerignore for `docker build -f mayhem/Dockerfile` (BuildKit prefers
# <Dockerfile>.dockerignore over the context-root file). Upstream's root .dockerignore drops
# build/** and dockerfiles/**, both of which hold TRACKED files (build/.empty, dockerfiles/*), so
# using it would bake a tree that differs from the commit. The commit image is a dev image: keep the
# FULL repo incl. .git history and drop only editor/OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
